const a = search({query:"append_progress"});
const b = search({query:"progress"});
return {a, b};

const summary = `STAGE: final answer, all three proposals scored; this record is the deliverable and stands on its own.
SCORE SUCCFAN-CURV-RQ: behavior=3 geometry=2 novelty=2 downstream=3 falsifiability=3 implementability=3 exploration=2. SCOPE IN_SCOPE (all five clauses met: fanout signal E1/E2, per-node curvature conformal factor E12/E13 in the residual recursion, three switches named). EVIDENCE E4 E5 E6 E8 E10 E11 E12 E13. Core reason: argmin_j||lambda r - c_j|| == argmin_j||r - c_j/lambda||, so the "curved" step is a per-item Euclidean radial dilation; lambda_p(0)=2 for all c_p, so the declared geometry-off limit c->0 gives lambda=2 not 1 and is not the plain-RQ control, and c_p=10 with ||x||=0.4 gives 1-1.6=-0.6 and lambda=-3.33 (sign flip, pole at 0.316). E5/E10 support the fanout heterogeneity strongly but E6 (curvature arms 0.0467-0.0550 vs Euclidean 0.0621-0.0636) and E8 (K=256 -> 0.0822 ceiling at level 1) pull against the flat-resolution hypothesis; exploration low because it is a small variation of an already-measured family.
SCORE cocond-markov-poincare-ot: behavior=4 geometry=3 novelty=3 downstream=4 falsifiability=3 implementability=3 exploration=4. SCOPE IN_SCOPE (transition matrix E1/E2, exp/Mobius/Poincare Sinkhorn cost + Einstein barycenter E12/E13, one assignment block). EVIDENCE E4 E5 E9 E10 E11 E12 E13. Core reason: E11 (same_first_prefix_rate 0.0907 vs permuted null 0.067) is the only SID-level measurement of the named problem; the strongest objection is scale - with batches of 1023 over 24556 items the in-batch successor probability is 1023/24556=0.0417 and the expected in-batch successor mass per row is at most 1-(1-0.0417)^5.45=0.21, so B_bt is near-identity and the run would test curvature, not coupling; the "5-8 MFLOP" budget only closes with a sparse operator (nnz 5600*256=1.43M per product, versus 2.7e8 dense).
SCORE CURVCELL-SID: behavior=3 geometry=3 novelty=3 downstream=4 falsifiability=3 implementability=4 exploration=3. SCOPE IN_SCOPE (per-cell branching E1/E2, curvature-rescaled Poincare distance in argmin and commitment E12/E13, behaviour->kappa->cell->behaviour loop). EVIDENCE E4 E5 E6 E8 E10 E12 E13. Core reason: the geometry arithmetic checks out - s=sqrt(kappa)=log(1+B)/((d-1)R) is the inverse-radius scale of curvature -kappa by the hyperbolic volume law log V ~ (d-1)R sqrt(kappa), so d_B/s is the metric of curvature -kappa, no cancellation - but the executed operation is a per-code scalar division that a per-code Euclidean temperature reproduces and no matched control is given; the fatal control defect is that B[l][k] enters only via kappa, so "geometry-off keeps the behaviour weights but removes curvature" is unimplementable and collapses to behaviour-off; and with uniform B the field is a global scale (H=log K, one s per level), which is reachable at K=256 given E8's 0.0822 co-cluster share.
Uncertainties: E12/E13 are truncated for all three bundles, so the assignment-score form of the conformal factor (SUCCFAN) and the alpha derivation (cocond, inside SAFEGUARDS) are UNKNOWN; the bounded checks are reading the frozen SPEC EQUATIONS / config. No ablation, sweep, seed repetition or Recall prediction is used anywhere.`;
const r4 = await tools.progress.append_progress({content: summary});
return r4;

